From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: quire <quire@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:02:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] optional net
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Feature `net` (on by default): the network of shared sessions (`inkboard-net`,
iroh) becomes optional for the web build. A page that embeds a board (feature
`embed`) has no use for it: `--no-default-features --features web-glow,embed`
leaves the session network out of the build, and the embedded board cannot
open a network connection.

Without `net` the web build uses `session_net_off.rs` (the settings stand-ins
the "Join" window and the shutdown call), installs no guest factory, refuses
every relay address (`platform::check_relay_url`) and does not offer "Join a
session…". The desktop always needs the network: building it without `net` is
a compile error. The public page keeps it: `web/Trunk.toml` lists it, and the
WebGPU build of `scripts/build_web.sh` and `build_web.ps1` names it too,
because a `--features` list on trunk's command line replaces the one in
Trunk.toml. So does the browser bench (`web-test` implies `net`).
